OpenClaw — https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw
MIT. The pinned revision is in runtime/upstream.json. Local modifications are
provided as source patches. The upstream license is retained in
runtime/LICENSE.openclaw and in every installed runtime.

openclaw-weixin — https://github.com/Tencent/openclaw-weixin
MIT. extensions/tencent-weixin is based on version 2.4.10, with local changes
for verified private routing, memory intake, reminder delivery, quota guards,
and multi-message replies. Tencent's license is retained at
extensions/tencent-weixin/LICENSE.

ClawX and SillyTavern were reviewed as design references. No source code from
those projects is included. Python and JavaScript dependencies retain their
own licenses in their installed distributions.

FastEmbed — https://github.com/qdrant/fastembed
Apache-2.0. Installed as a dependency; its distribution retains its license.
The default BAAI/bge-small-zh-v1.5 embedding model is MIT-licensed, downloaded
separately from https://huggingface.co/Qdrant/bge-small-zh-v1.5 into private data.
